                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Apparently Your Mother is on sale.\n>Opened mom\n>Opened cs2\n>Opened cases\n>Mom told me I was doing a good job\n>Lost 300€\n\n-Buys game\n-Able to say \"i bought your mother\"\n-Get 100% achievements\n-Able to say \"I 100%ed your mother\"\n\nGOTY material [Recommended 👍]\n\nA game where I can invite my friend’s mom? Finally, a true family drama simulator.\n\nThe multiplayer experience is something else. The more friends you have, the more moms you can invite. At some point, it stops feeling like a game and starts resembling an unexpected family gathering. The achievement system is also… unique. Spending \"30 minutes with a different mom\" doesn’t sound like a challenge—it sounds like a headline that could ruin your reputation.\n\nThe gameplay is disturbingly realistic. I invited my friend’s mom through Steam, and somehow she materialized in my room, told me to clean up, and gave me a life lecture. If that’s not peak immersion, I don’t know what is.\n\nThe only thing missing is a sequel called \"Your Father\", but just like in real life, I have a feeling it’s never going to be released.\nI love it when i'm playing any war themed game and just hear \"are you winning son\" in the background.\nmy whole life has lead up to this moment\n\n\nif your passing by you can pet this cat.\n\n　　　　 　 　 _ _\n　　　 　　／＞　　フ\n　　　 　　| 　_　 _ l\n　 　　 　／` ミ＿xノ\n　　 　 /　　　 　 |\n　　　 /　 ヽ　　 ﾉ\n　 　 │　　|　|　|\n　／￣|　　 |　|　|\n　| (￣ヽ＿_ヽ_)__)\n　＼二つ",
